<title>SWEDEN: Astra says contacts FDA on Pulmicort.</title>
<headline>Astra says contacts FDA on Pulmicort.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drugs company AB Astra said on Wednesday it had been in further contact with the U.S. Food &amp; Drug Administration (FDA) about approval for its anti-asthma drug Pulmicort.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been in touch a couple of times after the telephone conference (between Astra and FDA) in March,&quot; Astra spokesman Staffan Ternby told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;There have been questions, but they were solved as they came up so nothing is building up.&quot;</p>
<p>Astra still hopes to get approval this spring to be able to launch Pulmicort/Turbuhaler in the U.S. in the summer.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still too early to exclude a launch in the summer,&quot; Ternby said.</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
